values ('5e0c1f2a-0d4b-4c8e-9a1f-1d1c0a000004',$c$Nutriwoman Gestation$c$,$c$CA-NWG-30$c$,$c$Women’s Health$c$,$c$A complete nutritional formula for expecting mothers, throughout pregnancy.$c$,899,null,20,$c$/products/nutriwoman-gestation.jpg$c$,'50% 50%',true,$c$Nutriwoman Gestation is a complete nutritional formula for the whole of pregnancy. It brings together folic acid, zinc, vitamin D and the B vitamins and minerals an expecting mother's body draws on, so mother and baby are supported from the first weeks to the last.
Folic acid helps the body produce and maintain new cells. Zinc contributes to normal fertility and reproduction. Vitamin D is involved in calcium absorption, immune function and the protection of bones and muscles. Magnesium, iron and vitamin B3 contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue; vitamins B1 and B6 contribute to normal energy release; vitamins B2 and B12 contribute to the maintenance of normal red blood cell formation.

Uses
Folic Acid Support
Helps support new cell formation, which is why folic acid is recommended before and during pregnancy.
Healthy Pregnancy
Provides essential nutrients for mother and baby.
Energy Metabolism
Supports normal energy release through the tiring months.
Blood Formation
Helps maintain healthy red blood cell formation.
Bone and Muscle Health
Supports strong bones and healthy muscle function.
Immunity
Helps support immune health during pregnancy.

Nourishing motherhood, supporting new life
Pregnancy raises the need for several nutrients at once. One daily tablet designed for that stage is simpler and safer than stacking separate products, and it should always sit alongside the antenatal care your doctor provides.$c$,$c$Pregnancy • Folic acid • Energy • Immunity$c$,$c$Calcitamin • Ferrovix Fort$c$,$c$AM: Nutriwoman Gestation • PM: Calcitamin$c$,ARRAY[$c$Complete maternal formula$c$,$c$30 tablets$c$,$c$Halal certified$c$,$c$GMP facility$c$]::text[],$c${"benefits": [{"icon": "general", "title": "Folic Acid Support", "text": "Folic acid helps the body produce and maintain new cells."}, {"icon": "heart", "title": "Supports Healthy Pregnancy", "text": "Provides essential nutrients for mother and baby."}, {"icon": "energy", "title": "Energy Metabolism", "text": "Vitamins B1 and B6 contribute to normal energy release."}, {"icon": "general", "title": "Blood Formation", "text": "Vitamins B2 and B12 contribute to normal red blood cell formation."}, {"icon": "muscle", "title": "Bone and Muscle Health", "text": "Vitamin D supports strong bones and healthy muscle function."}, {"icon": "immunity", "title": "Immunity Boost", "text": "Helps support immune health during pregnancy."}, {"icon": "calm", "title": "Less Tiredness", "text": "Magnesium, iron and vitamin B3 contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue."}], "ingredients": [{"name": "Folic Acid", "amount": "", "purpose": "Helps the body produce and maintain new cells; a key nutrient before and during pregnancy."}, {"name": "Zinc", "amount": "", "purpose": "Contributes to normal fertility and reproduction and to normal immune function."}, {"name": "Vitamin D", "amount": "", "purpose": "Involved in calcium absorption and immune function; helps protect bones and muscles."}, {"name": "Magnesium, Iron and Vitamin B3", "amount": "", "purpose": "Contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue."}, {"name": "Vitamins B1 and B6", "amount": "", "purpose": "Contribute to normal energy release."}, {"name": "Vitamins B2 and B12", "amount": "", "purpose": "Contribute to the maintenance of normal red blood cell formation."}], "howToUse": ["Take one tablet daily with a meal, or as directed by your doctor or midwife.", "Start when planning a pregnancy if possible and continue throughout.", "Take iron-containing tablets away from tea, coffee and calcium supplements for better absorption."], "faqs": [{"q": "When should I start taking Nutriwoman Gestation?", "a": "Ideally when you start planning a pregnancy, and then throughout all three trimesters. Follow your doctor's advice."}, {"q": "Does it replace the folic acid my doctor prescribed?", "a": "Do not stop a prescribed supplement without asking your doctor; show them the pack so they can advise."}, {"q": "Can I take it while breastfeeding?", "a": "Ask your doctor or midwife; nutritional needs change after birth."}, {"q": "How many tablets are in a pack?", "a": "30 tablets, a one-month supply at one tablet a day."}], "safetyInfo": "• Food supplement, not a substitute for a varied diet and a healthy lifestyle.\n• Consult a healthcare professional before use if pregnant, nursing, taking medication or under medical supervision.\n• Do not exceed the recommended dose.\n• Keep out of reach of children.\n• Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight.\n• Contains iron. Keep out of reach of children; accidental overdose of iron-containing products is a leading cause of poisoning in children under six."}$c$::jsonb)
